1
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:05,088
♪ In the not-too-distant future

2
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:08,133
♪ Somewhere in time and space

3
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:11,303
♪ Mike Nelson and his robot pals

4
00:00:11,303 --> 00:00:14,848
♪ Are caught in an endless chase

5
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:17,226
♪ Pursued by a woman
whose name is Pearl

6
00:00:17,226 --> 00:00:20,729
♪ An evil gal who
wants to rule the world

7
00:00:20,729 --> 00:00:23,732
♪ She threw a few
things in her purse

8
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:25,317
♪ And in her rocket
ship she hunts him

9
00:00:25,317 --> 00:00:27,444
♪ All across the universe

10
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:30,239
I'll get you!

11
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:32,199
♪ I'll send him cheesy movies

12
00:00:33,075 --> 00:00:36,203
♪ The worst I can find,
la, la, la,

13
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:39,331
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all

14
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:42,584
♪ And I'll monitor his mind,
la, la, la,

15
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:45,379
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control

16
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:48,632
♪ Where the movies begin or end,
la, la, la,

17
00:00:48,632 --> 00:00:51,510
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity

18
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:55,472
♪ With the help of
his robot friends

19
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,183
♪ Robot roll call

20
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,768
♪ - Cambot
- you're on

21
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,311
♪ - Gypsy
- Oh my stars!

22
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,688
♪ - Tom Servo
- Check me out

23
00:01:02,688 --> 00:01:04,731
♪ - Croooow
- I'm different

24
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:07,359
♪ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes

25
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:10,570
♪ and other science facts,
la, la, la,

26
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:13,448
♪ Just repeat to
yourself it's just a show

27
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:16,868
♪ I should really just relax

28
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:21,832
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000

29
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:26,003
(clanging vibrations)

30
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:36,930
See what I mean?

31
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,598
Man, look at those things.

32
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:39,516
Do we tell him?

33
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:40,851
We have to.

34
00:01:40,851 --> 00:01:42,352
Mike? Get in here, Mike.

35
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:43,270
Mike? Oh, there you are.

36
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:44,563
Hey guys.

37
00:01:44,563 --> 00:01:46,023
Hi everyone, welcome to
the Satellite of Love.

38
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,065
Forget about that,
it's not important.

39
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,817
Mike, look at this.

40
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,319
Eew, yuck, what
are those things?

41
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:53,989
Those are eyelash mites.
They live in human eyelashes.

42
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:55,407
Yeah, you know,
I've heard of that,

43
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:58,285
it's a symbiotic thing where
they, little microscopic things

44
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:00,662
they feed off the dust and
debris of my eyelashes, yeah.

45
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:03,540
So you eat, and all
the food goes splashing

46
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,335
all over your face, and you
end up with monstrous demons

47
00:02:06,335 --> 00:02:08,337
feeding off the garbage
dripping from your eyelashes.

48
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:10,297
And you're okay with that?

49
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:11,715
Well, I mean, if you
put it that way it doesn't

50
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:13,258
sound so great.

51
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:14,676
I'm sorry, they gotta
go, we have got to get rid

52
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:16,261
of these things.

53
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,262
You guys, they're
really very small.

54
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,973
Oh, they're small,
meaning we don't have to

55
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:22,225
concern ourselves with the
other helpless creatures

56
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,269
undoubtedly living
in your eyelashes,

57
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:26,271
whole villages of
tiny, big-eyed children

58
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:28,690
being devoured by these dragons.

59
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:29,524
Is that in the article?

60
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:30,942
Yeah, it is.

61
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,235
You know what?

62
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:34,654
He likes having eyelash
mites, he enjoys

63
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:37,199
having meats and eggs
and sauces and saliva

64
00:02:37,199 --> 00:02:38,575
hanging from his eyelashes.

65
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:41,286
If you guys are that
concerned about it

66
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,579
we could probably have
the nanites, you know,

67
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:44,039
take a look at it.

68
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:45,457
Alright, I'll go
get the nanites.

69
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:46,416
Okay.

70
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:48,335
Is that big-eyed thing
in the article here?

71
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:49,419
'Cause I don't see that.

72
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:50,754
It might have been
another issue, I don't know.

73
00:02:52,047 --> 00:02:53,757
("MST3K Love Theme" plays)

74
00:02:57,928 --> 00:03:00,430
Never fear, Mike, the nanites'll
have those disease-ridden

75
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:04,351
little pests off of your
oil-soaked eyelashes in no time.

76
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:05,685
We're talking about a
little fracas here, right?

77
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:07,521
I mean, we're not talking about
a war or anything, are we?

78
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:09,898
No, no, no.

79
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:13,527
Well, well no, no, no, no, no.

80
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:15,445
Don't even say the
word "war", Mike.

81
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:18,323
We'll send in a few nanites
to act as a security force.

82
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:21,284
It'll really be more
like a police action.

83
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:24,329
It'll be more like we're
relocating your eyelash mites,

84
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,248
teaching them to live
somewhere better,

85
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:28,417
like on a dog's back or
the thigh of a squirrel.

86
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,459
Yeah.

87
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:30,544
Well if you guys
think my eyelashes

88
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:32,170
are really disgusting--

89
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,422
Oh, absolutely,
filthy, disgusting.

90
00:03:33,422 --> 00:03:36,425
Well, let's have the
nanites take a look at 'em.

91
00:03:36,425 --> 00:03:37,676
Alright, you're
gonna like it Mike.

92
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:39,219
Best thing that ever
happened to you, buddy.

93
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:42,013
Okay, nanites, are you
positioned on forehead ridge?

94
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:44,224
Sir, yes sir, troops
are in position.

95
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,059
Then if the weather
is right, initiate

96
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,478
Operation Gross Eye.

97
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:49,479
Sir, yes sir.

98
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:51,440
Let's rock and roll people.

99
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:54,359
Ooh, it is not going well.

100
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:56,069
Not well at all.

101
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,988
You gotta cut your
losses, Nelson.

102
00:03:57,988 --> 00:04:00,240
Hello, hello?

103
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,242
We're getting cut to
shreds in there, man.

104
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:04,953
We can't win this war, they
know the eyelashes too well.

105
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,705
What kind of an animal
called this war anyway?

106
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:08,206
Who could have done this?

107
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:09,916
Who? Just tell me who?

108
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:10,792
(crying out)

109
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:13,378
Ned, Ned the nanite.

110
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:16,506
- Oh Ned!
- Ned! Ned!

111
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:19,426
Oh, Nelson, why did
you want this war?

112
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:21,511
What? Was it about pride?
Tell us.

113
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:24,014
What, me?
You're the ones who forced me--

114
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,223
Save it, butcher.
Pearl's calling.

115
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:28,018
Ah, there's the click.

116
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:32,564
Some say it's imbued with
the power of Zeus himself.

117
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:33,523
Whatever.

118
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:36,276
Say, make yourself useful
and hook me one of these.

119
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,030
Hey loser.

120
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:42,282
I found out that
Bobo is the Mad Goth

121
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:45,285
and he's like these
Spartan guys' big hero

122
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:46,703
'cause he can kill
lions and stuff,

123
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,538
like big whoop, who can't?

124
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,373
Now they're throwing a
big party in his honor

125
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:55,128
and people aren't paying
enough attention to me.

126
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:57,589
Are you talking to your
little gods in the sky

127
00:04:57,589 --> 00:05:00,467
because no one else
will talk to you?

128
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:01,551
Slut, I mean, what?

129
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:02,511
(fanfare)

130
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:03,303
He's here!

131
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:05,430
The Mad Goth has arrived!

132
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,765
(applause)

133
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:08,934
Oh Cal, Cal, be a dear
and nip out for more mead.

134
00:05:08,934 --> 00:05:10,227
But I'm doing
the statue thing.

135
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:10,519
More mead.

136
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,811
Yes dear.

137
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:19,694
Thank you, thank you,
well who's got it going on?

138
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:22,239
We believe that you do.

139
00:05:22,239 --> 00:05:23,865
Aha, let me hear
it from you people.

140
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:26,243
We praise you and
we hold you high.

141
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:28,411
Aha, now that's what
I'm talking about.

142
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:30,872
Oh, I'm gonna be
ill, very, very ill.

143
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,666
Oh no, not the brain, oh please.

144
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,545
Oh, this is not good.

145
00:05:37,504 --> 00:05:39,548
Though Nelson
promised a quick return

146
00:05:39,548 --> 00:05:42,717
of the nanite forces,
the war for his eyelashes

147
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:45,470
lasted well into December.

148
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:48,557
Thousands were cut down
defending a blasted little patch

149
00:05:48,557 --> 00:05:51,643
of Nelson's T-zone
known as Follicle Hill.

150
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:52,936
Would you guys knock it off?

151
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:54,771
I mean, you're the ones
who wanted this war anyway.

152
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:57,315
It's too late to
apologize now, Mike.

153
00:05:57,315 --> 00:05:58,441
Right.

154
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:00,777
Hey, wait a minute, can't the
nanites just fix themselves?

155
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:01,736
Oh sure, no problem.

156
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:04,447
Well then what, ow, ow.

157
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,907
And in honor of
our beloved Mad Goth.

158
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,117
Thank you, thank you.

159
00:06:07,117 --> 00:06:10,662
We unveil this 40-foot statue.

160
00:06:10,662 --> 00:06:15,208
(awing and oohing)

161
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:19,254
Oh, look at the
definition, huh?

162
00:06:20,547 --> 00:06:22,799
Could have used a little
more marble in there,

163
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,759
but still a
creditable effort, eh?

164
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:27,220
(clapping)

165
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,389
Well, come on everybody,
let's go watch me eat.

166
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:31,182
Oh, let's do, let's do.

167
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:38,023
Well there you have it then.

168
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:41,234
It's time, I think.

169
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,154
Lovely.

170
00:06:44,154 --> 00:06:45,155
(singing)

171
00:06:45,155 --> 00:06:46,740
No, Brain Guy, no!

172
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:48,033
No!

173
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,284
I'm using this!

174
00:06:49,284 --> 00:06:51,036
Oh, no, no you're not.

175
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:54,873
Let's wait, Pearl.

176
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:56,541
Tempting as it is we must
delay our own suicides

177
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,835
and recapture Professor Bobo.

178
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,670
His reckless time
travel could rip apart

179
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,130
the universe itself!

180
00:07:03,465 --> 00:07:03,673
So?

181
00:07:04,758 --> 00:07:06,843
How to explain it
to the likes of you?

182
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,179
Okay.

183
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:12,349
Bobo ripples time itself,
the Nabisco company never

184
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:16,102
comes into being, no more
"Chicken In A Biskit".

185
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:27,739
Bobo's... messing... with my...
favorite... snack... cracker?

186
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:28,865
That's right.

187
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,116
Let's go.

188
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:30,742
Goddamn.

189
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:39,167
Oh, by the way, Mike,
Pearl told me to tell you

190
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:42,671
that your movie this week is
Invasion of the Neptune Men.

191
00:07:42,671 --> 00:07:43,254
Enjoy.

192
00:07:44,631 --> 00:07:45,256
See ya.

193
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:47,634
Eew.

194
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:51,721
Wow, jeez Mike, now your
eyes are a real mess.

195
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,765
Why'd you even get rid
of your eyelash mites?

196
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:54,724
You know, they're the things

197
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:56,601
that keep your eyelashes clean.

198
00:07:56,601 --> 00:07:59,145
Oh, we've got movie sign, I'll
deal with you two later.

199
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:01,856
(clanging vibrations)

200
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,452
Hey, look at that,
it's Oliver Reed's liver

201
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:16,162
encased in Lucite.

202
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:19,791
Oh, it's kind of
a gentle invasion.

203
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:20,583
Yeah the kind of
invasion you can

204
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:21,918
listen to all day.

205
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,756
Well, kids, the Hamilton
clock on the wall

206
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:29,300
tells us it's time for the
Invasion of the Neptune Men.

207
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,596
Wow, they blew their wad
on the title sequence.

208
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:37,726
I used to be
virulently anti-pix,

209
00:08:37,726 --> 00:08:39,310
but now I'm pro-pix.

210
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:42,480
Well, if it's not
too much trouble,

211
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,524
could somebody ritual
seppuku me right now, please?

212
00:08:47,569 --> 00:08:50,572
Sounds like the Little Rascals
are gonna be in this.

213
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:55,118
This must be the
national anthem of Neptune.

214
00:08:56,453 --> 00:09:02,000
Featuring Santa,
Speed Racer, Shonen Knife,

215
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,251
Sailor Moon!

216
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:10,717
Oh no, someone knocked
over the sump pump

217
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:11,760
in the Mir.

218
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:18,767
This is Runic two,

219
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,477
which reached the
moon the other day.

220
00:09:20,477 --> 00:09:21,478
Oh, boy.

221
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:24,230
I wish I'd been on it.

222
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,775
You were on it, Mr.
Tabana, weren't you?

223
00:09:26,775 --> 00:09:28,151
Of course he was.

224
00:09:28,151 --> 00:09:30,195
He worked on it
with Dr. Strauss,

225
00:09:30,195 --> 00:09:31,696
didn't you, Mr. Tabana?

226
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,406
Kid got off a good one, great.

227
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:37,535
D'oh! Now the Mir's fan
belt has snapped.

228
00:09:42,207 --> 00:09:43,500
Pretty exciting, isn't it?

229
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,793
Sure is!

230
00:09:44,793 --> 00:09:46,836
Well, children,
that ship was built

231
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:49,798
after Major Glenn's
spaceflight by Dr. Strauss

232
00:09:49,798 --> 00:09:52,801
and Dr. Tanowei, Kenny's father.

233
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:55,053
Major Glenn and I
are to be married.

234
00:09:55,053 --> 00:09:56,721
I merely assisted the others.

235
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:57,806
And worked on it.

236
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:00,809
Do you think you
and Kenny's father

237
00:10:00,809 --> 00:10:04,312
can design a spaceship
all by yourselves?

238
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:05,688
Why, sure.

239
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:06,856
Ow, my spine!

240
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,650
A scientist like
Dr. Tanowei can,

241
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:09,859
Mr. Tabana is his right arm.

242
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:11,361
Isn't that so, sir?

243
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:13,321
No.

244
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:15,657
We can work together.

245
00:10:15,657 --> 00:10:18,159
We're done, so you
can go out and play.

246
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:21,162
Go to Germany and play.

247
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:24,082
It's cram camp.

248
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:29,337
Come to the
Renaissance festival.

249
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,175
They're trying
to catch Mothra.

250
00:10:35,927 --> 00:10:38,346
Strange way to dry your bowls.

251
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:44,686
10:26, it's time the
satellite got here.

252
00:10:44,686 --> 00:10:45,603
Get moving, huh?

253
00:10:45,603 --> 00:10:46,354
Okay.

254
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:47,730
Swing it over more.

255
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:48,731
Alright.

256
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:49,983
How fast is the wind blowing?

257
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:51,109
18 miles an hour.

258
00:10:51,109 --> 00:10:52,235
Which way?

259
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:53,403
South-southeast.

260
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:55,113
Thank you for sewing
my hand to the tent.

261
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,282
Hey what is it?

262
00:10:57,282 --> 00:10:58,575
Any sign of it yet?

263
00:10:58,575 --> 00:11:00,702
Look at those two lovers.

264
00:11:00,702 --> 00:11:02,704
Jeez, they're all
over each other.

265
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:07,417
No one looks down
for a satellite.

266
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:09,127
I got mixed up.

267
00:11:09,127 --> 00:11:10,295
He's very young.

268
00:11:10,295 --> 00:11:10,962
Yeah.

269
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:12,088
And he's Japanese.

270
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:13,464
Ooh.

271
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:18,052
I invite you to
pull my finger.

272
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:19,596
Hey, the satellite has fallen!

273
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:20,805
Huh, what?

274
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,974
I'm sure it's the satellite,
it landed in those woods.

275
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:24,058
Come on, let's go!

276
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:28,479
Head for the Alps,
the border is closed!

277
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:33,359
Music courtesy of
Sergei Prokofiev.

278
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:38,031
We feel fresh.

279
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,660
These kids are like 10, so.

280
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,953
Yeah, they're
well out of college.

281
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,705
Shouldn't they
be at their jobs, then?

282
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:52,879
Ah, ooh, ow, oh, the sawgrass,

283
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:54,881
oh why did I wear
my little shorts?

284
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,303
Soldiers are
popping up everywhere

285
00:12:00,303 --> 00:12:01,888
asking if the war is over yet.

286
00:12:07,602 --> 00:12:09,562
Wonder if he's
been lapped yet.

287
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:10,772
He's in there, over there!

288
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,316
There's no satellite here.

289
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:14,943
But I saw it!

290
00:12:14,943 --> 00:12:16,778
It wouldn't come
down here, never!

291
00:12:16,778 --> 00:12:17,695
He imagined it.

292
00:12:17,695 --> 00:12:18,655
Yeah.

293
00:12:18,655 --> 00:12:20,657
Look, that's it!

294
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,075
Hey come on let's go!

295
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:23,826
Oh, I can see how
they missed that.

296
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,787
Prefab Lutheran church.

297
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:30,083
Ah, Allegra.

298
00:12:34,629 --> 00:12:35,922
A spaceship.

299
00:12:35,922 --> 00:12:37,882
It's not Runic Two!

300
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:40,760
Come on, there never
were two ships on Earth.

301
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,011
Why did it fall down?

302
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:42,679
What next?

303
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:43,638
Get over there!

304
00:12:43,638 --> 00:12:45,056
I wouldn't go.

305
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:46,683
Why not?
You found it, you know.

306
00:12:46,683 --> 00:12:48,017
I'm too scared to go.

307
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,644
He must be the
Piggy of the group.

308
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,944
How do we pickle it?

309
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:02,031
Look at the size of it.

310
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,158
That part there is
how you get into it.

311
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:07,662
(cries out)

312
00:13:07,662 --> 00:13:09,122
What's that?

313
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:10,665
Suppository Man.

314
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:16,421
Say, could you guys help me

315
00:13:16,421 --> 00:13:17,588
get this thing off my neck?

316
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:20,258
Don't worry kids,
it's a promotional

317
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:22,051
gimmick for Sushi Cereal.

318
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:26,347
Oh, hi, say, we're
looking for the Bullethead

319
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:27,181
family reunion?

320
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:33,021
Go that way, no,
go over there, wait,

321
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,939
now you fall down, good.

322
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:38,651
Ah, Kenny, Kenny, Kenny!

323
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:39,610
(yelling)

324
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,029
We're on gool.

325
00:13:41,821 --> 00:13:43,322
They have Braille helmets.

326
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:47,285
So the aliens
come and strangle

327
00:13:47,285 --> 00:13:49,495
little kids.
Thank you, Japan.

328
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:50,747
Nice.

329
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:53,666
So they all die and
the movie's over.

330
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:54,917
Oh good, alright.

331
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,671
And immediately Bob Hope

332
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:01,424
is flown in to
entertain the troops.

333
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:03,009
Tojo's death car.

334
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:06,763
(mumbling)

335
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:12,143
Run, get out of here.

336
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:13,061
You're in my
pickled eel garden.

337
00:14:13,061 --> 00:14:13,811
Get moving!

338
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:17,023
Come on, let's go!

339
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:18,149
Take us away, little shorts.

340
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:22,403
My baru barockers really work.

341
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:28,076
Ha ha ha ha ha, your costume
is ridiculous.

342
00:14:29,911 --> 00:14:31,496
Children of the pot.

343
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:35,625
La Toya Jackson.

344
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,295
Ha ha! Oh, sorry, I missed.

345
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:44,050
Ah, this guy trained
under Bruce Lee... bowitz.

346
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,887
Ah, ah.

347
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:49,055
Oh that guy just fell down,

348
00:14:49,055 --> 00:14:51,224
for crying out loud.

349
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:53,976
Ah, ah.

350
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:58,272
Waah.

351
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:03,986
Go Panthers!

352
00:15:09,117 --> 00:15:12,537
Oh, I rode my
bike to work today.

353
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:17,667
This is the set of Tattletales,
if I'm not mistaken.

354
00:15:17,667 --> 00:15:20,503
I just know Dr.
Smith's gonna be in this.

355
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:21,129
William.

356
00:15:22,255 --> 00:15:24,507
Well, I checked,
there's no toilet paper

357
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:26,050
downstairs either.

358
00:15:30,138 --> 00:15:32,640
We do have water
damage, don't we?

359
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:37,019
What the hell are
they doing out there?

360
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:42,066
I knew we shouldn't have
sent in the B-squad.

361
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:46,112
Jeez. Ronnie, Chad,
Bryce, get back in here.

362
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:49,115
They're being defeated
by a wispy bachelor.

363
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:54,954
A table saw on his head.

364
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:59,041
("MST3K Love Theme" plays)

365
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:08,050
Start the rockets
Ed, start the rockets!

366
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:12,388
Say, has anyone seen my record?

367
00:16:15,016 --> 00:16:17,768
We gotta go in,
but we'll be back.

368
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:20,062
Legalize it.

369
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,316
Oh come on, I
wanna jump around

370
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:25,067
while you fall down more.

371
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:30,114
(mumbles)

372
00:16:31,282 --> 00:16:32,116
Hey!

373
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,703
Oh, looks like the Russians
blew another reactor.

374
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:36,287
Yep.

375
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,125
(lightning striking)

376
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:44,128
Draw, storm.

377
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,632
What the hell'd I do that for?

378
00:16:49,634 --> 00:16:51,135
Playing is hard today.

379
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,020
Fine, fine, we'll just invade

380
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,271
somewhere else then.

381
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:06,067
Did you, oh, sorry,
I thought you said something.

382
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:10,238
Finally, this movie is over.

383
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:12,782
Did this one seem
really long to you guys?

384
00:17:12,782 --> 00:17:15,243
Actually, I don't
think it's over.

385
00:17:15,243 --> 00:17:18,120
This is the Neptunian
Bay of Pigs.

386
00:17:20,289 --> 00:17:22,041
(cheering)

387
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:23,042
Yay, they'll
park 10 miles away

388
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:25,002
and kill other people.

389
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:26,295
Grill's ready.

390
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,341
That's Space Chief.

391
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:33,135
Space Chief?

392
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:35,846
(cheering)

393
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:38,683
Hey, hey, hey,
don't touch the car.

394
00:17:38,683 --> 00:17:41,227
Thanks a lot for saving
us, that was great.

395
00:17:41,227 --> 00:17:42,311
The greatest.

396
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,188
Who are ya, mister?

397
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,940
Yeah, what's your name?

398
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:48,192
You boys picked one
that suits me fine.

399
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,277
Move back and let me go.

400
00:17:49,277 --> 00:17:51,279
How 'bout ineffectual
chicken-headed bachelor?

401
00:17:51,279 --> 00:17:52,571
Oh, boy.

402
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:00,955
He really cherried
out his golf cart.

403
00:18:02,665 --> 00:18:03,457
Space Chief.

404
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:07,128
That's Space
Chief, and he's real.

405
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:09,088
Space Chief, guys, he's real!

406
00:18:10,673 --> 00:18:13,301
He spins around
and strafes the kids.

407
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:17,096
Well, you know, it
wasn't really that bad.

408
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:18,764
At least it was short.

409
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:23,936
Am I supposed to eat this?

410
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,105
Oh father, can't you
take a rest and get to bed?

411
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,940
Where's Tabana?

412
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,900
He'll be coming soon.

413
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,402
I'm down 400 million yen.

414
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,696
What's your hurry, Papa?

415
00:18:33,696 --> 00:18:34,572
Oh.

416
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:37,116
What times are it?

417
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,367
(giggles)

418
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,286
You're going to be sick.

419
00:18:40,286 --> 00:18:42,163
That cold seems worse.

420
00:18:42,163 --> 00:18:44,582
I must put on
something decent.

421
00:18:44,582 --> 00:18:45,333
(knocking)

422
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:46,500
Hello.

423
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:49,337
See that wave band?

424
00:18:49,337 --> 00:18:52,089
Something's happening
to make it reverse.

425
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,220
It's over 200 maaahs!

426
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:00,222
What is it?

427
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:03,142
Probably some upset caused
by the flight of a satellite.

428
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:05,353
An extraordinarily
strong electronic wave.

429
00:19:05,353 --> 00:19:07,355
Our radar telescope
reported it, sir.

430
00:19:07,355 --> 00:19:09,273
Our men have been
picking up the band.

431
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,316
On the scope, eh?

432
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:11,859
Yes.

433
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,152
It's ultra short.

434
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:14,695
66 mega cycles, sir,
on the band.

435
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:16,322
The opera?

436
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:19,075
And yet it measures
about 18,000 kilowatts.

437
00:19:19,075 --> 00:19:20,284
The band's ultra short?

438
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:21,285
Where's it from, then?

439
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:23,579
Our electronic brain
stopped working immediately.

440
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:24,789
It just stopped?

441
00:19:24,789 --> 00:19:25,790
Yeah.

442
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:27,375
Much like our scene.

443
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,295
Another celebrity interview?

444
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:33,589
Darn it, I just can't
get a news break,

445
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,299
there's nothing happening.

446
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:37,426
Well there's the
dolphin-killing festival.

447
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:38,344
What?

448
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:41,847
The clock's running backwards.

449
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:44,183
That means lunch
won't be 'til yesterday.

450
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,979
(beeping)

451
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,272
It must be Santa's beeper.

452
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:56,404
(dance music)

453
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:58,531
Meanwhile, in
pre-revolution Havana...

454
00:19:59,657 --> 00:20:01,909
Is this what the
Japanese think we do?

455
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,331
Oh, it was such a great song.

456
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:10,167
Oh, let's go.

457
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:12,461
Hey, look.

458
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:16,465
Paul is a dead man,
miss him, miss him.

459
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:18,217
It's running backwards?

460
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:20,302
Who's been fiddling
around with this?

461
00:20:20,302 --> 00:20:22,513
What kind of a
machine is this?

462
00:20:22,513 --> 00:20:24,181
(beeping)

463
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,308
Not a very good
elk call, is it?

464
00:20:29,562 --> 00:20:31,021
(singing)

465
00:20:31,021 --> 00:20:32,731
That's weird, these
guys don't look Irish.

466
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,236
Hey, come on.

467
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:38,946
Did you leave a
yen on the track?

468
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:44,160
Do the Japanese practice
just in time railroad repair?

469
00:20:46,454 --> 00:20:47,455
What's going on?

470
00:20:47,455 --> 00:20:48,330
That engineer's crazy.

471
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:50,249
He's crazy.

472
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:51,959
What's he trying to do, crash?

473
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,335
Japan's only stupid guy.

474
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:56,172
(beeping)

475
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:11,145
Take over the
administration building.

476
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:13,481
What happened to
reverse the current, sir?

477
00:21:13,481 --> 00:21:16,484
Electrically operated industries
said their power failed.

478
00:21:16,484 --> 00:21:18,444
All our town sent in reports.

479
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:20,446
And that queer sound.

480
00:21:20,446 --> 00:21:23,449
An American satellite, one
might have been overhead.

481
00:21:23,449 --> 00:21:26,035
I will not answer that
until we have investigated.

482
00:21:26,035 --> 00:21:28,454
Doctor, this is not
a natural phenomenon.

483
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,414
A strong electronic
wave of unknown origin

484
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:32,500
did put our power supply
temporarily out of order.

485
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,751
Am I right?

486
00:21:33,751 --> 00:21:35,794
I'd say that you're correct.

487
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:39,381
Papa, space men,
we saw a whole bunch!

488
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:41,467
Really, and their
rocket ship, teacher!

489
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:44,053
It's different than
the Runic, honest!

490
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:45,513
Get the cane.

491
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:46,514
Where was this, son?

492
00:21:46,514 --> 00:21:47,765
Out near Mount Asaka.

493
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:49,517
We were there to
see the satellite.

494
00:21:49,517 --> 00:21:50,476
Well?

495
00:21:50,476 --> 00:21:52,019
We were caught
by the space men.

496
00:21:52,019 --> 00:21:53,687
But Space Chief
came and saved us.

497
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:54,563
Huh?

498
00:21:54,563 --> 00:21:56,190
Space Chief, huh?

499
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:58,692
We named him, he's the
greatest, the real thing.

500
00:21:58,692 --> 00:22:00,736
He got there in seconds.

501
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:02,530
Space Chief, eh?

502
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:03,614
A fighter?

503
00:22:03,614 --> 00:22:05,699
Yeah, we'll make
it a feature story.

504
00:22:05,699 --> 00:22:06,867
We told you the truth.

505
00:22:07,535 --> 00:22:08,536
Pencil drop.

506
00:22:08,536 --> 00:22:09,787
10 o'clock.

507
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:14,208
Well, back to the
national emergency, okay?

508
00:22:14,208 --> 00:22:16,293
Dr. Tanowei, how do
you see these things?

509
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:17,419
As scientific phenomena?

510
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:19,505
Tell us sir,
what's causing them?

511
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:20,214
Randy?

512
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:22,633
We knew you'd listen.

513
00:22:22,633 --> 00:22:24,260
You understand.

514
00:22:24,260 --> 00:22:25,511
Hey, that's a good one.

515
00:22:25,511 --> 00:22:27,054
Voices.

516
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,472
Tabana, I can see
you're not taking

517
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:31,058
all this space talk
seriously, are you?

518
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:34,478
Well, it's an
interesting idea.

519
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:35,479
Look Tabana.

520
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:37,106
What's going on?

521
00:22:37,106 --> 00:22:40,776
The power plant failed,
everything's stopped.

522
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,778
You see, you
know who did that?

523
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,613
Well, here's your news break.

524
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:46,407
Take those kids
out to Mount Asaka.

525
00:22:46,407 --> 00:22:47,366
Leave 'em.

526
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:48,993
Get a shot of
whatever's there.

527
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:50,494
It's nonsense, you know that.

528
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:51,745
Why not?

